    (property "Description" "" (at 1079.85 431.27000000000004 0)
      (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    )
    (property "Note" "6 mm^2 THT wire pad -> 5x10 mm SMD solder pad 2026-08-16, same reasoning as J1-J3 plus it removes a 4.4 mm hole from the phase node. The wire lies flat on the pad, which is exactly how the S50 [47] terminates its phases. ENGINEERING DEFAULT: 5x10 mm is KiCad's stock SMD wire pad, not a current-rated selection, and an SMD pad has no through-hole barrel helping carry current into the inner layers -- so the pad's via stitching to the phase pour matters more than before. Size against IPC-2152 [46] before fab." (at 1079.85 431.27000000000004 0)
      (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    )
    (pin "1" (uuid 3610cb99-bcb3-435d-b81e-a9b016bc540e))
